WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
When I came out of the prison of war, my friends, especially the younger ones,

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:13.400
who couldn't go to dance school, I practiced dancing with them at our house.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:30.800
I think this project has welded the whole class together very strongly.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.240
Yes, it could hurt me again, not before.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.040
It couldn't hurt you.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:41.080
My heart just goes up when I realize what it all does to people.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:46.920
A woman always said to me, don't shake your shoulders.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:52.000
Yes, of course we danced waltzes, especially Wiener waltzes left and right.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.680
When you introduced that project to us, it reminds me of the good feeling of my childhood.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.120
And since I grew up, every memory was bringing back to me.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:06.760
The youngest person on our project was 9 years old and the oldest was 96.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:14.160
I was on the dance floor for the first time at the age of 15 and never left again.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:21.080
Many of them could not remember their last dance.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.160
But because of the project, we could make their memories come back to life.

